- entry .SmartHttp   remote repositories over HTTP(S) by git's smart protocol, as `gitTransports.smartHttp`
+ entry .SmartHttp   repositorios remotos por HTTP(S) con el protocolo inteligente de git, como `gitTransports.smartHttp`

= entry .SmartHttp   remote repositories over HTTP(S) by git's smart protocol, as `gitTransports.smartHttp`
-   detail
+   detail

-       A `Transport` for the native backend: the capability advertisement is read from
-       `info/refs?service=…`, and each command is a `POST` to the service, with protocol
-       version 2 requested in the `Git-Protocol` header. Credentials in the URL's userinfo
-       (`https://user:token@host/…`) are sent as Basic authentication. It speaks through
-       whichever `Http.Backend` is in scope, so `SmartHttp()` needs one
-       (`httpBackends.javaNetHttp`, say), and `Native(List(SmartHttp()))` is a backend which can
-       clone, fetch and push over HTTP(S).
+       Un `Transport` para el backend nativo: el anuncio de prestaciones se lee de
+       `info/refs?service=…`, y cada orden es un `POST` al servicio, con la versión 2 del
+       protocolo solicitada en la cabecera `Git-Protocol`. Las credenciales de la información de
+       usuario de la URL (`https://user:token@host/…`) se envían como autenticación Basic. Habla a
+       través del `Http.Backend` que haya en el ámbito, así que `SmartHttp()` necesita uno
+       (`httpBackends.javaNetHttp`, por ejemplo), y `Native(List(SmartHttp()))` es un backend que
+       puede clonar, obtener y enviar por HTTP(S).

